{"version":"10.0","level":"5","subject":"en","questions":[{"id":"EN-5-06937","topic":"Vocabulary","difficulty":"sukar","question":"Which word means a place where doctors treat patients?","correct":"hospital","answers":["market","stadium","library","hospital"],"explanation":"The correct word is “hospital”.","concept":"vocab-3","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq","years":[3,5]},{"id":"EN-5-07099","topic":"Sentence","difficulty":"sukar","question":"Choose the correct sentence.","correct":"We are going to the market.","answers":["Are we going market the.","We is going market.","We going are the market.","We are going to the market."],"explanation":"This sentence has correct subject-verb agreement and word order.","concept":"sentence-1","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq","years":[3,5]},{"id":"EN-5-07087","topic":"Sentence","difficulty":"sukar","question":"Choose the correct sentence.","correct":"She likes reading books.","answers":["Likes she reading books.","She books likes reading.","She like reading books.","She likes reading books."],"explanation":"The subject and verb agree, and the word order is correct.","concept":"sentence-0","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq","years":[3,5]},{"id":"EN-5-07013","topic":"Tenses","difficulty":"sukar","question":"Tomorrow, we ___ visit the museum.","correct":"will","answers":["will","did","was","has"],"explanation":"“Tomorrow” indicates future time; “will” is appropriate.","concept":"tense-2","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq","years":[3,5]},{"id":"EN-5-07133","topic":"Comprehension","difficulty":"sukar","question":"Read: “Maya wakes up at seven o’clock. She eats breakfast before going to school.”\n\nWhat does Maya do before school?","correct":"She eats breakfast.","answers":["She eats breakfast.","She goes swimming.","She goes to bed.","She watches a movie."],"explanation":"The passage states that Maya eats breakfast before school.","concept":"comp-1","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq","years":[3,5]},{"id":"EN-5-06996","topic":"Tenses","difficulty":"sukar","question":"Yesterday, Amir ___ football.","correct":"played","answers":["played","play","plays","playing"],"explanation":"“Yesterday” signals past tense, so use “played”.","concept":"tense-0","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq","years":[3,5]},{"id":"EN-5-07157","topic":"Comprehension","difficulty":"sederhana","question":"Read: “Adam found a wallet and gave it to his teacher.”\n\nWhat quality did Adam show?","correct":"Honesty.","answers":["Carelessness.","Laziness.","Honesty.","Anger."],"explanation":"Returning a lost wallet shows honesty.","concept":"comp-3","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq","years":[4,6]},{"id":"EN-5-07101","topic":"Sentence","difficulty":"sukar","question":"Choose the correct question.","correct":"Where are you going?","answers":["Where is you going?","Going where you are?","Where you are going.","Where are you going?"],"explanation":"Questions with “you” use “are” before the subject.","concept":"sentence-2","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq","years":[3,5]},{"id":"EN-5-07152","topic":"Comprehension","difficulty":"sukar","question":"Read: “The pupils planted five trees behind the school. They water the trees every afternoon.”\n\nWhere did the pupils plant the trees?","correct":"Behind the school.","answers":["Beside a hospital.","At the market.","In the classroom.","Behind the school."],"explanation":"The location is stated directly in the passage.","concept":"comp-2","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq","years":[3,5]},{"id":"EN-5-07029","topic":"Tenses","difficulty":"sukar","question":"Last night, they ___ a movie.","correct":"watched","answers":["watching","watched","watch","watches"],"explanation":"“Last night” signals past tense.","concept":"tense-3","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq","years":[3,5]},{"id":"EN-5-06991","topic":"Grammar","difficulty":"sukar","question":"My sister and I ___ pupils.","correct":"are","answers":["was","are","am","is"],"explanation":"A compound plural subject takes “are”.","concept":"grammar-5","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq","years":[3,5]},{"id":"EN-5-07037","topic":"Tenses","difficulty":"sukar","question":"Now, the children are ___ in the park.","correct":"playing","answers":["play","plays","playing","played"],"explanation":"After “are”, use the -ing form for an action happening now.","concept":"tense-4","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq","years":[3,5]}]}